1. Develop a movie theatre booking simulator that manages a 3 × 3 seating grid layout. The
program should accept user row and column selections and change that seat's status
keyword from "O" (Open) to "X" (Reserved).



# Movie Theatre Booking Simulator

seats = [
    ["O", "O", "O"],
    ["O", "O", "O"],
    ["O", "O", "O"]
]

print("Initial Seating Layout:")
for row in seats:
    print(row)

row = int(input("Enter row number (1-3): "))
col = int(input("Enter column number (1-3): "))

if 1 <= row <= 3 and 1 <= col <= 3:
    if seats[row - 1][col - 1] == "O":
        seats[row - 1][col - 1] = "X"
        print("Seat reserved successfully!")
    else:
        print("Seat is already reserved.")
else:
    print("Invalid row or column.")

print("\nUpdated Seating Layout:")
for row in seats:
    print(row)
